### Why this fixes the UI
Your React code in VoucherPostingStatus.jsx is looking for specific strings to decide which Chip to show:
 * It looks for "SUBMIT" to show the creator's time. By passing "Submitted (Scheduled)", you trigger the isSubmission logic correctly.
 * It looks for "(SCHEDULED)" or "(Posted)". By ensuring these strings are passed, the React logic (rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("(SCHEDULED)")) will correctly identify that a schedule is active and stop defaulting to the "Immediate Execution" chip.
